// BT-3766, rewritten by BT-5150 (ADR 0153): a class-side `on:do:` in a loop
// whose protected block always raises. The class used to declare a class
// variable, which kept it in class-process mode and made every catch arm run
// the class-variable restore. With `classState:` gone it is a stateless class
// method that runs in the caller, so this row's number changes from the
// BT-5145 baseline. `SsbOnDoRaiseObject` is the instance-side control.

Object subclass: SsbOnDoRaiseClass

  class loop: n :: Integer -> Integer =>
    1 to: n do: [:i | [Error signal: "x"] on: Error do: [:e | 0]]
    n
